depgraph, PackageVirtualDbapi, PackageTracker: key the atom caches by the atom strings

Sub-series: A (probe, match and config memos) - patch 9 of 10; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Of these it needs 0001, 0002, 0005 only.

Five caches are keyed by (atom, atom.unevaluated_atom): the match caches
of PackageTracker, PackageVirtualDbapi and the composite db, the cross-run
match memo of patch 0002 and _highest_pkg_cache. An Atom hashes and
compares by its string through Python-level methods; for plain Atoms the
key now holds the two strings (_atom_key), which finds the same entries
without those calls. PackageVirtualDbapi.match() also skips dep_expand()
for a plain non-virtual Atom (it would return the atom as it is), and
PackageTracker.match() reads the slots of a plain Atom directly.

This was the first of the four pieces of patch 0021 of the 25-patch
ladder (atom-matching-caches). It is a patch of its own, in sub-series A,
because it changes the key of the match memo that patch 0002 adds, and
its _atom_key() helper is placed after the _ReplayIter class of patch 0005
(a dependency of place only: nothing of 0005 is used). The other four
caches are in unpatched 3.0.83. Not measured apart from the rest of 0021:
see there for the figures of the four pieces together.

Weak spots and what was not checked:
* Relies on Atom.__eq__/__hash__ using the string alone; subclasses keep
  Atom keys.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21; cut out of its
former patch on 2026-11-21 without changing a line of code. Not a
human-written change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on
six states of one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the
same merge list in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts
and the same package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
